  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IFPRI study on aflatoxin and child stunting links</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this reserach is to extend the evidence base on the association between dietary exposure to aflatoxin (highly posionous moulds found in maize and other crops) and child growth. The research uses a randomised controlled trial methodology to study the impact of an intervention aimed at lowering aflatoxin exposure among children from birth to 2 years of age in eastern Kenya.  Evidence of a causal relationship would be expected to catalyse significant additional funding to control aflatoxin as a strategy for tackling childhood undernutrition.</narrative>
  </description>
